---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Lightbox from "../components/Lightbox.tsx";
---

<Layout
  title="Jack Yu – Research"
  description="Research projects by Jack Yu, including photonics, lasers, and quantum computing."
  favicon="/favicon-external-tab.ico"
>
  <div class="content-wrapper">
    <section class="research-list">
      <!-- Raspberry Pi Camera Noir Project -->
      <div class="research-card">
        <h3>September 2025 - Raspberry Pi Near-Infrared Imaging</h3>
        <p>
          Unsatisfied with the awkward usage of IR viewers, I developed a camera system using the Raspberry Pi Camera Module 3 Noir, which is built around the Sony IMX708 sensor. Unlike the standard Pi Camera, the Noir version lacks an infrared filter, enabling us to capture near-infrared light. This makes it especially useful for visualizing and aligning laser systems in the near-IR range, many of which would otherwise be invisible to the naked eye. Combined with autofocus and a compact integration, the setup provides a lightweight, portable, and eye-strain-free alternative to traditional infrared viewers. To operate the system, I used the libcam library to write a GUI in python.
        </p>
        <p>Click on images to enlarge.</p>

        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem;">
          <figure class="bio-figure">
            <Lightbox src="/images/picam1.jpg" alt="Pi Camera Noir setup view 1" client:load />
            <figcaption>Camera can be setup in many impossible angles</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="bio-figure">
            <Lightbox src="/images/picam4.jpg" alt="Infrared imaging example" client:load />
            <figcaption>3D printed articulating mount</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="bio-figure">
            <Lightbox src="/images/picam2.jpg" alt="Pi Camera Noir setup view 2" client:load />
            <figcaption>Display saves space</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="bio-figure">
            <Lightbox src="/images/picam3.jpg" alt="Captured near-IR laser alignment" client:load />
            <figcaption>Portable setup (at probe station)</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="bio-figure">
            <Lightbox src="/images/picam5.jpg" alt="Compact Pi Noir camera integration" client:load />
            <figcaption>Selfie taken with camera (12MP)</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>


      <div class="research-card">
        <h3>Snapshots from Summer 2025</h3>
        <p>
          I worked on a mechanical fixture to AR coat a Lithium Niobate
          waveguide, and built a U-bench external cavity setup. At the same
          time, I set up a raspberry Pi near-infrared camera system with
          autofocus, which is more convenient that using an infrared viewer.
        </p>
        <p>Click on images to enlarge.</p>

        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem;">
          <!-- AR coating fixture -->
          <figure class="bio-figure">
            <Lightbox
              src="/images/AR-coat.png"
              alt="AR coating fixture SolidWorks model"
              client:load
            />
            <figcaption>AR coating fixture (SolidWorks)</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="bio-figure">
            <Lightbox
              src="/images/AR-coat-irl_compressed.jpg"
              alt="Tangible AR coating fixture"
              client:load
            />
            <figcaption>Tangible AR coating fixture</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <!-- U-bench SolidWorks image -->
          <figure class="bio-figure">
            <Lightbox
              src="/images/U-bench.png"
              alt="U-bench SolidWorks model, view 1"
              client:load
            />
            <figcaption>U-bench model (SolidWorks, view 1)</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>


      <!-- Senior Project 2025 -->
      <div class="research-card">
        <h3>Senior Project – Fall 2025</h3>
        <p>
          My senior project was to set up an External Cavity Diode Laser (ECDL),
          to ultimately characterize AR coatings on gain chips. Along the way, I
          machined many custom optomechanical components, including flexure
          attachments, and a custom mount for AR coating in a Veeco Spector.
        </p>
        <p>Click on image to enlarge.</p>

        <figure class="bio-figure">
          <Lightbox
            src="/images/250512vFJACKSENIORPROJECTPPT_40x30.jpg"
            alt="Senior Project Summary Slide"
            client:load
          />
          <figcaption>Senior Project Summary Slide (Summer 2025)</figcaption>
          <figcaption>
            <a
              href="/images/250512vFJACKSENIORPROJECTPPT_40x30.pdf"
              target="_blank"
              style="color: dodgerblue; text-decoration: underline;"
            >
              Open full-resolution image
            </a>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <!-- 2024 Etalon Summary -->
      <div class="research-card">
        <h3>Etalon Characterization & Summary 2024 Research Summary</h3>
        <p>
          Conducted Fabry–Pérot etalon measurements and compiled a general
          summary of my 2024 research into this slideshow, which I presented to
          my department.
        </p>
        <p>My data and experiemtal setup was presented to DARPA.</p>
        <div class="research-links">
          <a
            href="/documents/2407JUL24_Etalon_and_General_Summary.pdf"
            target="_blank"
            style="color: dodgerblue; text-decoration: underline;"
          >
            View PDF Slides
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
